course: dictionary
lesson: 4044
title: Gemstones: precious stones
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A gemstone is a stone that people think is precious or beautiful, and it is cut and polished so that it sparkles. Look at the words around a new word to work out what it means.
explain: «A gemstone is a stone people cut and polish because it is beautiful, rare and hard enough to last.» The clues are cut, polish, beautiful and rare. A gemstone is not just any stone: someone has shaped it so that it shines.
explain: Try the swap check. Put «precious stone» in place of gemstone and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, your meaning is right. Diamonds, rubies, sapphires and emeralds are all gemstones.
explain: «A gemstone is a mineral, or sometimes a material like amber...» Amber is not a mineral, so this sentence shows that gemstone covers more than one kind of material. When the context is not enough, use a dictionary.
fact: A gemstone is a precious or beautiful stone that is cut and polished for jewellery.
fact: Examples of gemstones are diamond, ruby, sapphire and emerald.
fact: Most gemstones are minerals that formed as crystals deep in the Earth.
fact: A gemstone's colour often comes from tiny amounts of other elements mixed into it.
fact: A birthstone is a gemstone linked with the month you were born.
exercise: «A gemstone is a stone people cut and polish because it is beautiful, rare and hard enough to last.» What is a gemstone? | Any stone found on the beach | *A stone that is cut and polished because it is beautiful and rare | A metal used for building bridges | A wooden toy shaped like a ring
exercise: Which of these is a gemstone? | Cardboard box | *Ruby | Pebble from the seaside | Brick from an old wall
exercise: Why does a gemstone often have its colour? | *Tiny amounts of other elements are mixed into it | It was painted by a jeweller | It has been left in the sun for a day | It is made from sugar
test: «The king's crown sparkled with precious gemstones.» What does gemstones mean here? | Dusty old bricks | Soft sweets | *Cut, polished stones that are precious and beautiful | Wooden beads
test: A birthstone is a gemstone linked with the month you were born. What is a birthstone? | A stone that can be eaten | A coin from a faraway country | *A gemstone linked with the month you were born | A type of cloud
exam: Use the swap check on «She wore a ring with a sapphire gemstone.» Which phrase fits best in place of gemstone? | Wooden spoon | *Precious stone | Soft cloud | Hot drink
